WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>The Old Man and Fish</b>

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.290
Shinobu-chan, you froze.

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:44.420
Is something wrong? That's not like you.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.020
I am honestly happy that Nobu didn't

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.370
suffer any damage from that case before,

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:55.420
but I'm just kind of not quite 
satisfied or something...

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:58.820
Well, things can't exactly 
continue without any change.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:01.050
Yeah, I guess so.

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:04.040
<b>Nobu's special eel bento</b>

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:04.930
Backeshof's plan was averted,

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:08.050
<b>Gernot (37)
 Tax Collector
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:08.050
but that does not change the fact that 
lager is still a prohibited good.

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:12.820
You should probably voluntarily refrain 
from serving any whatsontap for a while.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:17.020
Oh, and as usual, I'll 
have three eel bentos.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.140
I hate to do this to our customers,

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:25.400
but we'll have to give up 
serving beer for a while.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.620
Welcome!

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:28.190
Welcome!

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.200
<b>Previous Emperor (78)
The previous emperor of the empire</b>

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.200
<b>Johann Gustav (30)
Count of Badenburg</b>

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:30.190
Johann-san!

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.080
It has been a while. Please take a seat.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:36.070
It's uncharacteristically empty today.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:41.580
Apparently, the upcoming big conference 
has the whole city on edge.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:43.550
Maybe it's because of that.

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:45.290
I see.

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:47.580
That's really horrible for a bar.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:51.080
Well, we're going to take advantage 
of that to give you the best service.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.230
Here's your hand towel.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.730
Oh, that's nice and cool.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.510
Last time I was here, it was warm.

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:02.650
You change it based on the season, do you?

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:04.560
It is quite hot outside.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.300
Here is an appetizer.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.090
What is this?

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.610
<b>Young Mackerel Nanbanzuke</b>

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.610
<b>This pickled fish is delicious all the way down to 
the edible bone! The chili pepper gives it a good kick!</b>

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.600
It's nanbanzuke made with young mackerel.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.600
The mackerel is first fried,

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.460
then pickled in a sweet and sour 
marinade, then set aside to cool.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:17.390
It's perfect for this hot weather.

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:18.890
Hum.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:25.620
<b>Cool</b>

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.900
This is really good, Johann.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.680
Yes, Grandfather.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.360
The sourness is going to help 
with the lack of appetite

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.750
that is usual for hot summers.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:38.300
At first, I thought that pickling 
something fried is foolish,

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.000
but I suppose cooling it allows 
the oil and the acid to meld,

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.390
creating a gentle and smooth sourness.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:46.830
But I think it may be this 
hidden spiciness that's

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:49.270
tying the entire dish together?

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.670
You are correct.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.560
It's a chili pepper that 
we call hawk's claw.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.720
Hawk's claw, you say?

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:58.350
That sounds like a spice that's 
worthy enough for you, Grandfather.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:00.400
This may be a lucky omen.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:00.940
Hm?

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:02.940
By the way, Fräulein,

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:08.000
it seems that this dish is too 
good to enjoy without any drink.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.330
Right, what would you like?

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.390
What was it called again?

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:15.850
Whatsthatale? No, whatsonale?

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:17.810
Do you have an ale that sounds like that?

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:20.830
You mean whatsontap.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:24.670
I'm really sorry. Due to certain 
circumstances, we are not serving it right now.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.490
Could not you make an exception for me?

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:29.820
I came here because of that.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:32.840
We have heard about the commotion 
that Backeshof stirred up.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:38.270
But would it not be possible to accommodate 
my grandfather who's traveled so far?

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:39.600
Understood.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:40.830
Taishou?

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:43.790
Shinobu-chan, I thought about it,

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.510
but I just want our customers 
to enjoy themselves.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:49.100
Right!

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.710
Here you go. The two 
draft beers you ordered.

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:56.870
<i>The two draft beers you ordered.</i>

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:02.500
<i>This. This is it. Without 
this, it's not Izakaya Nobu!</i>

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:06.990
<i>This was the last piece my heart 
needed to feel fulfilled!</i>

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:10.640
Shinobu-chan was the one who wanted 
to serve this more than anything.

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:13.870
<b>Whatsontap</b>

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:13.870
<b>If it tastes good, then all is well...</b>

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:13.040
This is the whatsontap.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.200
Well then.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:17.970
<b>Fizz</b>

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:29.880
This is too funny.

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:34.270
You said there was someone who claimed 
that this is the empire capital's lager.

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:37.660
Yes, I heard it was a 
merchant called Backeshof.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.880
I don't know what he knows about lager,

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.730
but this is something different from 
the lager that comes from the capital.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.170
So it's ale?

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:49.080
No, it's probably lager.

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:54.160
But the lager they make in the capital 
has a more encompassing taste,

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:57.900
while whatsontap has a cleaner aftertaste.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.220
You sound like an expert.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.180
Not really.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:06.450
Since you can discern that sort 
of difference, this one is on us.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:07.770
Enjoy your draft beer!

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:11.050
<i>Draft beer, draft beer, draft beer.</i>

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.290
I'll deduct that from your pay.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:17.640
You should have another as well.

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:19.750
Let's eat and drink well tonight.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:20.300
All right.

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:23.070
What would you like to eat, then?

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:25.340
We'll trust you, so just 
bring out what you like.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:26.310
Understood.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:28.530
Well then, let's do this again.

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:31.040
Prosit!

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.760
Thank you for waiting.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:33.780
<b>Fried Mackerel</b>

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:33.780
<b>Cover it with plenty of sauce and bite it like a savage!</b>

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:36.540
This is fried mackerel.
Please enjoy it with this sauce.

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:40.040
They make you put the sauce on yourself.

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:42.310
That's an interesting thought.

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:44.660
Grandfather,

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:48.440
these look quite big. 
I shall cut them for you.

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:51.580
Fried mackerel must not be 
eaten with proper manners.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:56.670
Taking a huge bite like this is the 
secret way it tastes the best!

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:58.950
Taking a huge bite, huh?

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:00.470
<b>Crunch</b>

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:03.050
I have not done that in so very long.

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:04.840
<b>Crunch</b>

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:12.490
This airy and crispy breading becomes 
one with the oil, the sauce,

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:15.110
and the light flavor of mackerel meat!

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:18.680
Biting it like that is the 
right way, little miss.

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:19.360
Yes!

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:29.050
Speaking of, I heard people still eat

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:31.860
with their hands in the 
three northern territories.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:36.830
Yes, I believe someone from the entourage 
of Windelmark was quite upset

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:41.140
that they had been embarrassed 
at a banquet in the capital.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:46.420
I suppose the sum of such small 
differences is leading to ill feelings.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:47.880
Thank you for your patience.

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:49.390
This is flounder boiled in soy sauce!

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:52.770
Oh my, flounder in Aitheria.

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:54.900
And such a magnificent specimen, too.

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:03.390
I am so sorry!

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:06.730
I-I'm so sorry! The precious food!

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:08.760
Did you get hurt?

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:10.730
I am fine, but she's...

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:13.370
I'm sorry! This is horrible.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:14.900
Are you all right?

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:18.670
Let's make sure you didn't get burned.

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:22.020
You can have this. Soak it with 
water and cool your hands.

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:24.410
Th-Thank you so much.

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:27.610
Many apologies for that.

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:28.910
Do not worry about that.

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:32.260
However, it is too bad about the flounder.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:34.990
I will prepare another one right away.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.480
Please give me a few moments.

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:37.030
What?

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:40.410
After seeing such a magnificent flounder,

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:43.400
it does not behoove us to have high 
expectations for the next one.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:49.840
With this dish, letting it cool allows 
the flavor to seep in deeper.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:52.020
Since this one is bigger,

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:54.730
I was not so sure the flavor 
had gone deep enough.

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:56.290
But it looks like it will be good now.

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:58.700
U-Unbelievable.

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:01.060
An even bigger flounder.

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:05.150
It is comparable to the heart 
of a knight facing a dragon,

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:13.640
knowing that an even bigger dragon 
is waiting behind the first.

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:15.800
Very well.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:19.940
Let us enjoy this splendid 
flounder together.

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:23.950
Amazing! The fillet is so large 
that it does not fit on the plate.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:26.440
So let's cut that in half.

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:28.450
Here you go, Grandfather.

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:31.320
<b>Juicy</b>

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:39.900
<b>Juicy</b>

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:40.290
<i>I've never had flounder seasoned this way,</i>

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:43.130
<b>Juicy</b>

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:43.240
<i>but the sweet and savory flavors 
have permeated the entire fish.</i>

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:46.360
Sir, it seems you enjoy fish.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:50.110
If you have a request, we will prepare 
something to make up for before.

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:54.980
You know, in the fishing 
town that I grew up in,

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:57.840
we used to eat salt-cured salmon a lot.

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:01.620
Salmon? I do believe we have some.

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:06.860
Actually, the seared skin of 
that is my favorite food.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:09.470
Ah yes, that skin is delicious.

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:10.870
I will prepare some.

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:14.370
I never knew that something like 
that was your favorite food.

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:17.120
The skin will not fill you up.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:20.000
Some people insist that 
it should be thrown away.

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:24.600
But unless you try it, you won't 
know that it's a shame to do so.

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:27.550
Are you going to worry about 
what others say and discard it,

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:30.210
or are you going to understand 
its true nature?

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:33.130
The empire is the meat of the salmon,

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.750
and the northern territories are the skin?

00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:36.780
Well...

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:38.520
Thank you for waiting.

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:41.030
<b>Seared Salmon Skin</b>

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:41.030
<b>Salmon skin really is delicious, isn't it?</b>

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:41.020
This! This is it!

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:43.900
<b>Crunch</b>

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.800
Nothing beats the umami and 
aroma of fatty salmon skin!

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:52.170
It's the best snack for drinking!

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:59.510
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:58.920
Please come again soon!

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:04.230
We need to rescind the imperial order 
that makes lager a prohibited good.

00:10:04.230 --> 00:10:05.340
Grandfather!

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:09.100
Well, consider it a reward for 
the delicious salmon skin.

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:10.900
Thank you so much!

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:15.170
Johann, aside from the imperial order, 
there is something I need you to do.

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:16.000
Yes?

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:19.470
I'd like to make a change to 
the food menu for the conference

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:21.990
the day after tomorrow.

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:31.290
Next up, we've got Nobu Plus.

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:43.760
<b>Shinbashi</b>

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:37.710
So, we've come here to Shinbashi.

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:40.320
It could be considered a sacred 
place for employed folks.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:43.750
There are a sickening amount of bars here,

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:45.440
and watching Izakaya Nobu reminded me.

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:49.730
<b>Kenichi Nagira</b>

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:46.000
Reminded you of what?

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:49.210
That I am Japanese. It's just gotta be fish.

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:49.930
Oh, that's what you mean.

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:51.160
Should I just follow my instinct?

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:53.420
No, I'll show you a good place!

00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:57.950
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:56.710
Kenichi Nagira is going to go around the bars

00:10:56.710 --> 00:11:00.020
here to find the amazing 
dishes featured in "Nobu."

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:00.440
<b>Kenichi Nagira's search for the "Nobu" bar</b>

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:03.280
You know, you told me it was a side street, 
but there are too many of them.

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:06.160
<b>Kenichi Nagira
 Born in Tokyo's Ginza. Made his debut in 1970 as a folk singer.
 Since then, he's been active as an actor, celebrity, essayist.
 Has been in multiple shows that take place in bars or Shitamachi</b>

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:06.170
And since I keep looking up 
and down, I'm all dizzy.

00:11:06.160 --> 00:13:29.090
<b>Shinbashi 
Fish cuisine</b>

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:07.720
We're almost there!

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:08.270
It's here.

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:10.080
See? I told you.

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:11.460
I found it!

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:13.620
Hamankora is a place where you 
can enjoy fresh fish that's

00:11:12.120 --> 00:11:16.620
<b>Free diving fisher's fresh 
fish restaurant, Hamankora</b>

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:16.630
been sent directly from Kumamoto 
prefecture's Amakusa fishing harbor.

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:21.900
<b>Hamankora 
Nakajima Yuuko-san</b>

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:18.740
I'm grateful. I love these kinds of places.

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:19.490
See?

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:20.810
Welcome. Thanks for coming.

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:21.620
Thank you.

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:25.990
When I look around, all I see is 
Amakusa, Amakusa, Amakusa, Amakusa.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:29.390
My husband sends the fish from Amakusa.

00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:31.600
So you have fresh Amakusa fish here?

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:31.900
Yes.

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:33.210
And your husband is always there?

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:35.290
Yes, he dives and sends it here.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:35.950
Is he a surfer?

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:37.060
Why would you even ask that?

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:38.670
No, he is a free diving fisherman.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:39.530
So not a surfer.

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:41.610
No, he's not a surfer.

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:46.870
The thing she's going to make for us 
today is this white fish sashimi!

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:50.140
This is a stingfish.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:53.210
A stingfish? That's an excellent specimen!

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:53.490
Right.

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:54.110
Really, so magnificent!

00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:54.830
I agree.

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:57.990
You can be amazed later. Have some.

00:11:57.990 --> 00:12:00.420
How about that flavor, that texture?!

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:01.700
This almost crunchy texture...

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:02.940
Right, it's got that texture.

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:04.000
It's incredible.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:07.130
It's a fun experience for 
the teeth, too. Delicious.

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:07.000
Right.

00:12:07.130 --> 00:12:08.350
I love how fresh these are!

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:11.040
And this is the liver of the stingfish.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:14.290
You can hardly get this in Tokyo. 
How is that precious liver?

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:15.100
How is it?

00:12:15.980 --> 00:12:17.660
I'm so jealous!

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:17.660
It's good.

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:18.160
I want some!

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:18.900
These are eggs?

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:19.660
Yes.

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:22.480
I've not really seen stingfish 
eggs before, but these are big.

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:25.250
Really, this is the first 
time I've seen them, too.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:30.540
So, how do they taste? I'm jealous.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.050
These are so nice.

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:35.060
Of course! I can tell from your smile.

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:34.890
The skin?

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:36.340
Right, the skin.

00:12:36.340 --> 00:12:39.020
So you just eat the skin.

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:38.160
Collagen.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:41.030
I mean you do the same with blowfish, too.

00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:41.490
It's great for your skin, too!

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:41.770
This is safe to eat, right?

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:42.670
It's fine, yes.

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:43.410
How rude!

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:46.620
Don't say, "Oh, that Nagira ate it," afterwards.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.530
Stop saying things like that!

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:51.220
Oh, the skin might be the most delicious.

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:52.350
See?

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:52.650
So soft.

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:53.920
I was surprised.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:55.480
I want to try some too.

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:56.440
Then we have this.

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:58.130
Right. It's a sea snail.

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:01.430
This snail can be caught 
all around the country.

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:03.500
It resembles the hoof of a horse, 
so it's sometimes called

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:08.870
horse snail, but it has over 200 other 
names as well, like Pfeiffer's top shell.

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:10.620
Oh, you really know your stuff.

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:12.740
Yeah, I'm not... horsing around.

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:14.970
Oh, that was nervous laughter.

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:20.450
I didn't know about this place, but I 
am going to come here regularly now.

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:22.070
I look forward to that.

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:27.020
Even Nagira-san approves of "Free diving 
fisher's fresh fish restaurant, Hamankora."

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:29.090
<b>Assistance: Gurunabi                                 To be continued</b>

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:29.090
It's a two minute walk from Shinbashi Station.

00:13:29.090 --> 00:13:32.080
If you want to enjoy the true taste 
of fish, come here, come here!

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:57.980
